  "summary": {
    "as": "Introduced in Senate",
    "asOf": "2025-09-03",
    "date": "2026-10-21T19:18:42Z",
    "text": "Empower Parents to Protect their Kids Act of 2025\n\nThis bill prohibits an elementary or secondary school from receiving federal funds unless the school notifies parents about a student's gender identity and obtains parental consent for any associated school accommodations.\n\nAmong other requirements, school employees may not withhold information from parents about a minor student's purported identity that is incongruent with the student's sex, the student's discomfort with their\u00a0sex, or the student's desire to undergo a gender transition procedure. Schools must also obtain parental consent before proceeding with any accommodations for such students. The Department of Justice or a parent or guardian may bring a civil action against a school for violations."
  },
